<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Empress Elisabeth returns one week after her first visit, on the day of her consultation with Dr. Haddad-Lindström. She took thiamine daily and has eaten most of the 1,600 kcal meal plan, finding the evening meal hardest. She did not have the blood test that was due three to four days after the meal plan started, because she left for four days at a spa and no laboratory was arranged there. She has walked about two hours a day instead of five and has not used the rings or wall bars. Her ankles are a little more swollen in the evenings. She still feels dizzy when she stands quickly. She has had passive thoughts of being better off dead on a few days, with no intent or plan, and she has her safety plan. She has weighed herself at home each morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Meal plan</td><td>Most of 1,600 kcal a day; evening meal hardest</td></tr><tr><td>Thiamine</td><td>Taken daily</td></tr><tr><td>Missed test</td><td>Electrolytes due at three to four days not drawn</td></tr><tr><td>Exercise</td><td>Walking about two hours a day; no gymnastics</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Passive thoughts on a few days; no intent or plan; safety plan carried</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

